WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:15.476
At the beginning of summer vacation, everyone in town was talking about two things:

2
00:00:15.477 --> 00:00:21.350
the spectacular finale to the school's end-of-year recital and Muff Potter's trial.

3
00:00:21.351 --> 00:00:29.076
After his book had been torn, Mr. Dobbins became very quick-tempered, and he often used his whip on the children unjustly.

4
00:00:29.077 --> 00:00:32.723
Tom and the other schoolchildren had decided to get some revenge.

5
00:00:32.724 --> 00:00:36.631
Unknown to most of the town, Mr. Dobbins was bald.

6
00:00:36.632 --> 00:00:39.139
He hid his baldness with a wig.

7
00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:43.809
The plan was to expose Mr. Dobbins' baldness to the whole town.

8
00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:47.223
Tom thought the plan was good, but not good enough.

9
00:00:47.224 --> 00:00:50.790
He felt it needed something extra special.

10
00:00:50.791 --> 00:00:56.641
The night before the recital, Tom and several other boys slipped into the teacher's bedroom while he was sleeping.

11
00:00:56.642 --> 00:01:03.357
The boys knew that the teacher enjoyed several shots of whiskey before going to bed, and this made him a deep sleeper.

12
00:01:03.358 --> 00:01:08.678
The boys carefully painted Mr. Dobbins' bald head gold.

13
00:01:08.679 --> 00:01:11.409
The next evening Tom asked Huck to help.

14
00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:17.152
During the recital Huck cast his fishing line through the open window and snagged the teacher's wig.

15
00:01:17.153 --> 00:01:21.938
As the teacher was making his closing remarks, Huck reeled in his fishing line.

16
00:01:21.939 --> 00:01:31.644
The wig flew off, and the teacher's gold head was exposed.

17
00:01:31.645 --> 00:01:37.002
Everyone agreed it was a historic ending to the recital.

18
00:01:37.003 --> 00:01:40.993
The other event on everyone's mind was Muff Potter's trial.

19
00:01:40.994 --> 00:01:45.791
Whenever anyone mentioned it, or the murder, chills ran down Tom's spine.

20
00:01:45.792 --> 00:01:51.484
One day Tom went to Huck and asked, "Have you told anyone about what we saw?"

21
00:01:51.485 --> 00:01:54.151
"Of course not," replied Huck.

22
00:01:54.152 --> 00:01:58.201
"Why, Tom, we wouldn't be alive two days if that got out.

23
00:01:58.202 --> 00:02:01.366
Injun Joe would kill us."

24
00:02:01.367 --> 00:02:06.412
Tom relaxed. "I guess we're safe as long as we keep quiet."

25
00:02:06.413 --> 00:02:12.077
The boys promised again that they wouldn't say anything to anyone about Doc Robinson's murder.

26
00:02:12.078 --> 00:02:18.100
"Muff Potter is going to die!" said Tom.

27
00:02:18.101 --> 00:02:21.240
"He is," replied Huck sadly.

28
00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:24.533
"Don't you feel sorry for him?" asked Tom.

29
00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:30.219
"Yes," Huck said. "Muff may be a drunk, but he isn't a murderer.

30
00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:33.568
He's stood by me when I was out of luck."

31
00:02:33.569 --> 00:02:37.803
"He's fixed my kites plenty of times," added Tom.

32
00:02:37.804 --> 00:02:41.674
"I wish we could get him out of trouble."

33
00:02:41.675 --> 00:02:44.891
"The only way to do that is to talk.

34
00:02:44.892 --> 00:02:49.076
But if we talk, we'll be dead," said Huck.

35
00:02:49.077 --> 00:02:52.711
Tom and Huck did the only thing they could do to help Muff.

36
00:02:52.712 --> 00:02:57.859
That was to pass tobacco, matches, and other things to Muff through the window of his cell.

37
00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:03.743
Muff was grateful, but the visits only made Tom more depressed.

38
00:03:03.744 --> 00:03:08.340
On the day of the trial, the whole town gathered in the courthouse to watch.

39
00:03:08.341 --> 00:03:14.692
The prosecution called many witnesses to the stand, and none of them said anything good about Muff Potter.

40
00:03:14.693 --> 00:03:20.996
Even Muff's lawyer didn't defend him, and the prosecution was able to quickly build a solid case against him.

41
00:03:20.997 --> 00:03:25.060
The judge decided to break early for lunch.

42
00:03:25.061 --> 00:03:28.942
Tom knew that Muff would be hanged if he didn't say anything.

43
00:03:28.943 --> 00:03:33.126
He pulled Muff's lawyer aside as everyone was leaving the courtroom.

44
00:03:33.127 --> 00:03:37.183
Tom and the lawyer talked rapidly in hushed voices.

45
00:03:37.184 --> 00:03:44.170
When the trial resumed after lunch, the judge asked Muff Potter's lawyer if he had any witnesses that he wanted to call.

46
00:03:44.171 --> 00:03:50.045
The lawyer looked at the judge and said, "Yes, I would like to call Thomas Sawyer to the stand."

47
00:03:50.046 --> 00:03:54.388
The courtroom buzzed like a hive of bees as everyone whispered.

48
00:03:54.389 --> 00:03:59.801
After the oath was administered, the lawyer asked Tom where he had been on the night of the murder.

49
00:03:59.802 --> 00:04:05.259
Tom was about to answer when he saw Injun Joe staring at him.

50
00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:08.951
Tom, suddenly afraid, stammered his answer.

51
00:04:08.952 --> 00:04:13.397
"I . . . I . . . was in the graveyard."

52
00:04:13.398 --> 00:04:18.398
Tom explained that he had been hiding behind the large tree near Hoss Williams' grave.

53
00:04:18.399 --> 00:04:24.136
The lawyer then showed the court the bag of Indian herbs that the boys had left behind.

54
00:04:24.137 --> 00:04:26.358
The courtroom was silent.

55
00:04:26.359 --> 00:04:31.592
"How close were you to the murder that you witnessed?" the lawyer questioned Tom.

56
00:04:31.593 --> 00:04:36.181
"I was about as close as I am to you, sir," said Tom.

57
00:04:36.182 --> 00:04:39.729
"Can you describe to us exactly what you saw?

58
00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:44.859
Start at the beginning and don't leave anything out," cautioned the lawyer.

59
00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:47.128
Tom started his story.

60
00:04:47.129 --> 00:04:51.709
It was hard to speak at first, but soon words began to flow.

61
00:04:51.710 --> 00:05:01.200
He described Doc Robinson knocking out Muff with a rock and continued, "I saw Injun Joe grabbing a knife and—"

62
00:05:01.201 --> 00:05:06.072
Suddenly there was a loud crash. Injun Joe was gone.

63
00:05:06.073 --> 00:05:14.846
He had jumped through the courtroom window!
